      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Dry-run sandbox preserves symlinks that can redirect writes outside the sandbox",
      "description": "`copyInstallPaths` copies existing install paths while preserving symlinks. If a copied path (for example, `.claude` or a file beneath it) points outside the sandbox, the installer can follow that link and modify the real target during a dry run. This violates the promise that the project is never touched and can also make the change report omit the resulting modification. Avoid preserving writable symlinks in the sandbox, or otherwise ensure installer writes cannot escape it; add a regression test using a symlink to an external sentinel.",
